{% comment %}
  Tungacea — Specimen Card fields resolver.

  Reads the product metafields and echoes one delimited payload the shared
  product card splits apart:

    specimen_id || kreuzung || specs || status_state || status_label

  The card markup is unchanged; only what fills its slots is. Slot 2 used to
  hold a typed parentage string and now carries the cross, inherited from the
  referenced mother plant. Slot 3 used to hold trait and stage and now carries
  the three numbers a buyer actually needs before clicking: stage, leaf count
  and leaf length. A wrong expectation about size is the most common reason a
  rare plant arrives to disappointment.

  Availability is derived from Shopify itself. The former free-text status field
  matched only English substrings, so a status typed in German fell through to a
  neutral state — that whole class of mistake is gone with the field.

  Kept as a dedicated snippet so the shared card stays within Theme Check's
  Liquid complexity budget.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign mf = product.metafields.custom

  assign specimen_id = mf.specimen_id.value | default: '' | strip

  comment
    The cross comes from the mother plant entry, so it is entered once and every
    clone of that mother inherits it.
  endcomment
  assign kreuzung = ''
  assign mutter = mf.mutterpflanze.value
  if mutter != blank
    assign kreuzung = mutter.bezeichnung.value | default: '' | strip

    comment
      A mother plant is usually named after the cross, and so is the product,
      plus a running number. The card would then print nearly the same line
      twice. Both are reduced to bare letters and digits before comparing, so
      that a times sign, an apostrophe or a trailing number does not hide the
      duplication. If the title already carries the cross, the extra line goes.
    endcomment
    assign titel_norm = product.title | downcase | replace: '×', 'x' | remove: 'anthurium' | remove: ' ' | remove: '#' | remove: "'" | remove: '"' | remove: '-' | remove: '.'
    assign kreuzung_norm = kreuzung | downcase | replace: '×', 'x' | remove: 'anthurium' | remove: ' ' | remove: '#' | remove: "'" | remove: '"' | remove: '-' | remove: '.'
    if kreuzung_norm != blank and titel_norm contains kreuzung_norm
      assign kreuzung = ''
    endif
  endif

  comment
    F- and S-numbers and Species are read the same in both languages and pass
    through unchanged. Only the admission that nobody knows needs translating.
  endcomment
  assign generation = mf.generation.value | default: '' | strip
  if generation == 'Unbekannt'
    assign generation = 'products.product.specimen.generation_unknown' | t
  endif

  assign stage_label = ''
  case mf.stadium.value
    when 'Steckling'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_cutting' | t
    when 'Sämling'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_seedling' | t
    when 'Jungpflanze'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_young' | t
    when 'Etabliert'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_established' | t
    when 'Mutterpflanze'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_mother' | t
  endcase

  comment
    The three facts a photograph cannot carry: how far along the plant is, which
    generation it belongs to, and its size. Leaf count was dropped — it is
    countable in the pictures and was taking a slot from something harder to see.
    A length of zero would be nonsense, but the test for nil is kept so a real
    zero could never vanish silently.
  endcomment
  assign spec_parts = ''
  if stage_label != blank
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: stage_label | append: ' · '
  endif
  if generation != blank
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: generation | append: ' · '
  endif
  if mf.blattlaenge_cm.value != nil
    assign leaflen = 'products.product.specimen.leaf_length_short' | t: cm: mf.blattlaenge_cm.value
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: leaflen | append: ' · '
  endif
  assign specs = spec_parts | split: ' · ' | join: ' · ' | strip

  if product.available
    assign status_state = 'available'
    assign status_label = 'products.product.specimen_status.available' | t
  else
    assign status_state = 'sold'
    assign status_label = 'products.product.specimen_status.sold' | t
  endif
-%}
{{- specimen_id }}||{{ kreuzung }}||{{ specs }}||{{ status_state }}||{{ status_label -}}
